sushila gemire owns a store in the heart  of tamil kathmandu's tourist and  business hub she and her family have  remained safe from kovid but the virus  has hit business hard core  kovid has hurt us people are afraid to  come out  the bars and clubs are closed and even  if they were open people wouldn't come  during the second wave last year the  delta variant was killing hundreds of  people  hospitals were running out of oxygen  cylinders and intensive care beds  this time the omicron strain which is  more transmissible is spreading to the  community health experts say it is  infecting nearly every household in the  valley but hospital admissions and  fatalities are significantly lower nepal  experienced a surge in covid cases this  week with more than 10 000 people being  infected every day it's a record daily  high for the country since the start of  the pandemic the government projects  that daily infections may double by the  end of this month and has implemented a  series of measures to curb the surge the  kathmandu district administration office  suspended major services after a number  of its staff contracted covid including  the chief district officer  we are focused on discouraging mass  gatherings in large crowds and instead  encouraging people to follow government  health protocols  schools are shut till the end of the  month and frontline workers are  receiving booster doses gatherings of  more than 20 people are banned and masks  are mandatory outdoors people will need  vaccine cards to enter public spaces and  to access public services the third wave  has infected health workers in hospitals  and health care facilities in large  numbers  the previous wave left our health care  system in shambles we were unable to  cope with the overwhelming number of  patients this time we have to look out  for our health professionals who are the  backbone of the system  only 40  of nepal's 30 million people are fully  vaccinated fifty percent have received a  partial dose  with a relatively low vaccination rate  experts say nepal should expand its  vaccination drive mask up and maintain  social distance ramyata limbu al-jazeera  kathmandu
 

